pCloud Drive on Gentoo
======================
This packages the official amd64 pCloud Drive AppImage intact at
/opt/pcloud/pCloud.AppImage (with /usr/bin/pcloud). Portage owns upgrades;
never run the in-app updater or application as root. Removing this package
preserves user configuration, credentials, synchronized files, and any
application-created autostart entries.

Running as a user service
-------------------------
Use `agentoo cloud-storage pcloud start|stop|status` (see `--help`) to manage
pCloud via a transient systemd user service (`agentoo-pcloud.service`)
independent of your terminal. Disable "Start pCloud Drive on system startup"
in pCloud's own settings when using service management. Inspect logs with:
    journalctl --user -u agentoo-pcloud.service -b

Sync and virtual drive notes
----------------------------
- FUSE 2 (`/dev/fuse`) is required even when using local-folder Sync only.
- In 2.3.1, Add Sync cannot select the cloud root (`/`): create an empty local
  directory outside `~/pCloudDrive` for each top-level cloud folder and add a
  separate sync pair.
- The virtual drive always mounts at `~/pCloudDrive` (changing `fsroot` does
  not persist across restarts). To access it elsewhere, create a local symlink
  pointing to `~/pCloudDrive` while keeping `~/pCloudDrive` in place.
- Upstream's vendor launcher passes `--no-sandbox` to Electron; this package
  preserves that behavior intact.
